<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Wellness and Mindfulness – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Wellness and Mindfulness</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How Exercise Helps My Body</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Follow instructions in educational videos. Interactive: Respond to questions in group discussions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can follow instructions in educational videos on exercise routines (e.g., "Demonstrate a stretching routine often used before school sports events.") Can respond to questions in discussions about wellness habits (e.g., "I practice mindfulness because it helps me relax and focus better on my studies. It makes me feel calm and peaceful.") Can answer questions about the benefits of mindfulness (e.g., "Relaxation is important because it reduces stress and makes you feel better.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 30px;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f0f8ff;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 55%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 10%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of key vocabulary related to exercise and wellness.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of people doing various exercises (e.g., walking, stretching, running) and engaging in mindful activities (e.g., meditating, deep breathing). Students briefly share what they see and how the activities make them feel. The teacher asks: "What do you think these people are doing for their body?" and "What makes a body feel strong and healthy?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces 8-10 core vocabulary words related to the theme using flashcards and gestures: <em>wellness, mindfulness, exercise, energy, benefits, strength, flexibility, health, body, routine, practice</em>. The teacher clearly models pronunciation, focusing on stress in multisyllabic words like "flexibility" and "mindfulness." For example, the teacher says "mindfulness" slowly, emphasizing the first syllable, and repeats it several times. The teacher also models sentences using the Present Simple, such as, "Exercise <em>boosts</em> my <em>energy</em>." or "<em>Mindfulness</em> has many <em>benefits</em> for mental <em>well-being</em>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the new vocabulary.</p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I can touch my toes easily, what word describes my body?" (Expected answer: "Flexibility.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I focus on my breathing to relax, what am I practicing?" (Expected answer: "Mindfulness.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content through an authentic audio/visual resource, setting the context for the listening skill focus.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short (2-3 minute) educational video titled "Quick Morning Stretches for Energy and Focus" demonstrating an exercise routine. The video includes instructions like "Now, stretch your arms up," "Breathe deeply," and explanations of benefits using target vocabulary. </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening to understand the main points and specific details of an educational video on exercise routines and their benefits for mental and physical well-being.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (First listening - Gist):</b> Students watch the video once without taking notes. The teacher asks:</p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is the main idea of the video?" (Expected: How exercise helps your body get energy and focus.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What type of activities are they doing?" (Expected: Stretches, breathing exercises.)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Second listening - Specific details):</b> Students watch the video again. The teacher provides a simple True/False handout or prompts questions orally.</p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"True or False: The video says stretching boosts your mental well-being."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does the video say about flexibility and strength?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Focused practice on listening for accuracy and reinforcing target grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for specific instructions and benefits. Using Present Continuous (e.g., "I am stretching") and Present Simple (e.g., "Exercise improves health"), collocations (e.g., "energy boost," "mental well-being"), and vocabulary (e.g., <em>strengthen, relax, promote, balance</em>). Pronunciation practice on minimal pairs /ʊ/ and /uː/ through specific phrases.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: decimal;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Gap-fill Listening):</b> The teacher plays specific short segments of the video again. Students listen and complete sentences with words heard (e.g., "This routine can ______ your flexibility and ______ your body." or "Right now, we are ______ deeply to ______ our minds."). The missing words are selected from the target vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Sentence Building):</b> In pairs, students receive sentence starters related to the video's content and new vocabulary. They complete them using either Present Simple or Present Continuous based on the context. For example: "The instructor always ______ (promote) stretching before activity." or "We ______ (practice) mindfulness by ______ (breathe) slowly." Teacher monitors pronunciation, specifically distinguishing /ʊ/ and /uː/ in words like "could" (short u) and "suit" (long u) if encountered, or through specific drills if time allows (e.g., "He could wear a suit to the meeting.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Listening and Matching):</b> The teacher plays 3-4 audio snippets (short phrases or sentences from the video or teacher-created). Students listen and match each snippet to a specific benefit or instruction from a provided list. For example, a snippet might say, "This movement strengthens your core," and students match it to "Builds strength."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">12-15 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students actively use the target language in a realistic context, focusing on fluency and interaction.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion – "Our School Wellness Routine"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). The teacher prompts them with: "Based on what we watched and learned, how can exercise and mindfulness help students at our school? What specific actions can we take to promote mental well-being and physical health?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students discuss ideas for a "School Wellness Routine," sharing their wellness practices and suggesting solutions. They must use at least five vocabulary words from the lesson (e.g., <em>benefits, focus, relaxation, routine, promote</em>) and practice using Present Simple and Present Continuous.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They should aim to use pragmatic functions like "I exercise three times a week to stay fit and focused." and "Some people like to meditate because it helps them manage stress."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group prepares 2-3 suggestions to share with the class.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Example contribution:</b> "I am practicing short meditation daily to improve my focus for studies. It gives me an energy boost." or "A good morning stretching routine promotes flexibility and helps us feel calm before classes."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher circulates, listening to discussions, providing support, and noting use of target language and pronunciation (especially multisyllabic word stress).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment to gauge student understanding and application, followed by self-reflection.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group discussions. Focus on listening comprehension demonstrated through relevant contributions, and oral production of target vocabulary and grammar.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their 2-3 wellness suggestions to the class. Students listen to each other's presentations and the teacher asks follow-up questions to individual students based on the group discussion, such as "What is one benefit of mindfulness that you discussed?" or "Why is daily exercise a good habit for our body?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Listening Comprehension:</b> Student responses reflect understanding of video content and group discussion.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Incorporates at least 3-4 target vocabulary words (e.g., <em>wellness, benefits, energy, focus, relax</em>).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Uses Present Simple and Present Continuous correctly in responses.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible Pronunciation:</b> Clear pronunciation, particularly on multisyllabic words like "mindfulness" and "flexibility."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Cohesion:</b> Responses are clear and logically connected.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a slip of paper:</p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned that exercise and mindfulness ______ (verb: boost, improve, relax) my ______ (noun: energy, body, mental well-being)."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new word I can use to talk about health is ______ (vocabulary word) because ______."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson's effectiveness and preparation for subsequent lessons.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of the exercise video was easiest to follow? What was most challenging to understand?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did listening to the video help you understand the benefits of exercise for your body and mind?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; list-style-type: disc;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this listening-focused lesson? (e.g., The educational video was engaging, the vocabulary introduction was effective).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson? (e.g., Provide a vocabulary list in advance for students who struggle with listening for new words; spend more time on minimal pair drills if confusion was observed).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did students demonstrate their ability to follow instructions and respond to questions through listening?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will encounter a reading text (e.g., a short article or blog post) about "Healthy Habits for a Balanced Life" that incorporates the same key vocabulary words (<em>wellness, mindfulness, exercise, benefits, routine</em>) and grammar structures, building on their current understanding of the theme.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>